Package: softcats
Type: Package
Title: Regression on Predicted Categories with Calibrated Probabilities
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Marcell T.", "Kurbucz", email = "m.kurbucz@ucl.ac.uk",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0121-6781")),
    person("Economic and Social Research Council", role = "fnd",
           comment = "Grant UKRI5718")
  )
Description: Estimates the association between an outcome and a latent
    categorical group from calibrated class probabilities instead of
    predicted labels. Assigning each observation its most likely category or
    thresholding the probabilities distorts regression estimates (for a
    binary group it typically attenuates them) and can give confidence
    intervals whose coverage is far below the nominal level. The estimator
    partials the controls out of the outcome and the probabilities with
    cross-fitted machine learning nuisance functions and solves a
    Neyman-orthogonal moment equation, with heteroskedasticity- or
    cluster-robust standard errors and optional weights. Further functions
    report how much information the probabilities carry beyond the controls,
    test conditional calibration and direct effects of classifier features on
    labelled data, recalibrate the probabilities on such data, bound the
    bias from calibration error, and compare the estimate with hard-label
    regressions, including the distortion and the implied coverage of the
    cross-fitted hard-label estimate. Methods follow
    Kurbucz (2026) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2608.11784> for several categories and
    coarsening, Kurbucz (2026) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2605.12780> for confidence
    thresholding, and the cross-fitting of Chernozhukov et al. (2018)
    <doi:10.1111/ectj.12097>.
